$ is the *difference* of $B$ and $A,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in $B$ but *not* in $A.$\n\nThe elements of $B$ that are also in $A$ are $12,24,36,$ and so on (i.e. multiples of $12$). So, we must remove these elements from $B.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B∖A & =B-A \\\\  & =\\{6,12,18,24,30,36,…\\}-\\{4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32,36,…\\} \\\\  & =\\{6,18,30,42,54,…\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435968 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435966 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435968 #edb/ref 1069 "q-105225" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435968 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435968 #edb/ref 1071 "If $A=\\{10,20,30,40\\}$ and $B=\\{5,10,15,20,25,30,35,40\\},$ then $A∖B=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435968 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4c3c70ee-1d92-5844-ac72-dec994a61cf8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435968 #edb/ref 1074 "The set $A∖B$ is the set of all elements belonging to $A$ but *not* $B.$ Note that the elements $10,20,30,40\\in B$ are also in $A,$ so we must remove them. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A∖B & =A-B \\\\  & =\\{10,20,30,40\\}-\\{5,10,15,20,25,30,35,40\\} \\\\  & =∅.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435969 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186435973 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435969 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1027d02c-0636-540f-93cd-5d017fa6f5ef" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435969 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186157789 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435970 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "12b37427-ab27-5dc9-97aa-afad8b49dce5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435970 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186435967 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435971 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186435972 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435971 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2829e46f-848c-572e-8425-ea6cc5d2f217" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435971 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186435968 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435972 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 175